 772:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****         (##) HAL_SMARTCARD_AbortTransmitCpltCallback()
 773:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****         (##) HAL_SMARTCARD_AbortReceiveCpltCallback()
 774:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c **** 
 775:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****     (#) In Non-Blocking mode transfers, possible errors are split into 2 categories.
 776:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****         Errors are handled as follows :
 777:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****        (##) Error is considered as Recoverable and non blocking : Transfer could go till end, but e
 778:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            to be evaluated by user : this concerns Frame Error,
 779:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            Parity Error or Noise Error in Interrupt mode reception .
 780:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            Received character is then retrieved and stored in Rx buffer,
 781:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            Error code is set to allow user to identify error type,
 782:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            and HAL_SMARTCARD_ErrorCallback() user callback is executed. Transfer is kept ongoing on
 783:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            If user wants to abort it, Abort services should be called by user.
 784:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****        (##) Error is considered as Blocking : Transfer could not be completed properly and is abort
 785:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            This concerns Frame Error in Interrupt mode transmission, Overrun Error in Interrupt
 786:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            mode reception and all errors in DMA mode.
 787:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            Error code is set to allow user to identify error type,
 788:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c ****            and HAL_SMARTCARD_ErrorCallback() user callback is executed.
 789:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c **** 
 790:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_smartcard.c **** @endverbatim
